In the heavy quark limit, we examine the ratios of decay widths for $B_c$ and $B_s$ mesons in the context of certain decays, specifically $B_c 	o D_s \ell  ar{
u}$, $B_c 	o D_s \mu  ar{
u}$, $B_c 	o D_s \pi \ell  ar{
u}$, and $B_s 	o K \ell  ar{
u}$, $B_s 	o K \mu  ar{
u}$, $B_s 	o K \pi \ell  ar{
u}$, and $B_s 	o K \pi \mu  ar{
u}$. We find that these ratios deviate from the expected values of 1, 0.997, and 0.997, respectively, by 1.5%, 0.5%, and 0.5%. This deviation is a result of the finite mass of the heavy quarks involved in the decays.
